WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.537
Each team will have five minutes
to pitch, everybody knows that.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:07.540
They will then have five minutes
for questions and answers

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.109
after their pitch.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.045
The 15K Creative
Arts Competition

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:15.314
is for student arts
focused businesses.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.950
So this is an area of
arts entrepreneurship

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.688
that tends to mix the
arts and technology

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.890
and sciences up in
very interesting ways.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.524
Well, first of all,
I think MIT is just

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:27.227
an incredibly creative place.

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.829
There are so many
creative people here.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:33.999
I remember as a student, just
thinking that, in a sense,

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:35.901
art was everywhere.

00:00:36.001 --> 00:00:38.838
As a woman of color and as
a citizen in this earth,

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.773
I have some concerns.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.143
The parameter for
applying is really just

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:46.445
to have an idea, even if
you're a solo entrepreneur.

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:49.482
Because after you apply, there
are six weeks of mentoring,

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:53.386
and networking, and workshops,
so that at the end of April,

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.689
at Live Pitch Day, you have
a strong business plan,

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.257
you've considered
your market, you've

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:01.227
considered your past market,
you considered your team,

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.062
your value prop, and
all of the other things

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.030
that an important business has.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:09.669
The mentorship component really
helped us rethink some of our--

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.838
the way we're presenting
our ideas, and even

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.740
some of our business
model questions.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.940
So that was really helpful.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.844
I think the most important
thing is not the result.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:22.047
It's the process
during the competition.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.317
We're seeing a lot of
technological disruption

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.318
in the arts.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.720
And MIT being a
leader in technology,

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.390
it just needs to be
involved in supporting

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.658
the arts from a
technological perspective.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:35.395
[music playing]

